---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 1,
        "name": "Home",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 2,
        "name": "Services",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/services"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 3,
        "name": "Analytics Strategy Roadmap",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/analytics-ai-strategy-roadmap"
      }
    ]
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Decide what analytics work comes first | Alluvium"
  description="You already have Power BI or Excel. The roadmap names what your team should do first, and what can wait."
  canonicalPath="/analytics-ai-strategy-roadmap"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="service-fold">
<article>
<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><a href="/services">Services</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span>Analytics Strategy Roadmap</span></nav>
<p class="kicker">Analytics Strategy Roadmap</p>
<h1>Decide what analytics work comes first</h1>
<p class="lede">You already have Power BI, and you may still run the business from Excel. What you need is an order of work. We name what to do first, and what can wait.</p>
<p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
</div></header>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
<h2>Every team wants a report, and nobody has ranked them</h2>
<p>Finance wants a view of the close. Operations wants a view of the week. The board wants a pack. Each request is reasonable on its own, and the team starts whichever one arrived last.</p>
<p>The roadmap names the numbers a meeting will actually use, the data those numbers depend on, and the requests that do not change a decision yet. Your own people can staff that list.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="band band-alt"><div class="wrap">
<h2>The work that comes first, and the work that waits</h2>
<p>Your team staffs the work on the path first. Requests that do not change a decision stay off to the side until that work is done.</p>
